Translation patch: <PolyEncoder>::from_pb

Change: `core::array::from_fn` becomes array literals; the loop over `pts.chunks_exact(2)` becomes
an index loop; the `let s = if .. else if .. else ..` with an early `return` inside becomes
straight-line early returns.
Why: `array::from_fn` and `chunks_exact` are not modelled by the Aeneas Lean library, and the
`?`/`return` inside a loop nested in a value-producing `if` does not translate.
Behaviour: identical (only the initial capacity of `v` is `pts.len() / 2` instead of
`pts.len()`).
Relies on: `pts.len()` is even (checked just above), so there is no remainder.

